Verapamil hydrochloride extended-release tablets are a medicament in dosage form, so they fall in heading 3004. Verapamil is a phenylalkylamine, so the relevant subheading is 3004.90. The HTSUS 3004.90 statistical suffixes are mostly for "other" medicaments, and I recall 3004.90.9220 as "Other: for the treatment of hypertension" (not certain). I believe the 3004.90.92 breakout is "Other" with 10-digit lines such as 3004.90.9215 (antiasthmatics), 3004.90.9219, 3004.90.9221, 3004.90.9250 and others. I recall 3004.90.9240 as "Other: cardiovascular" or similar, but I'm not sure of the exact line.

Verapamil is a cardiovascular drug. I could not verify the exact 10-digit line, so I'm choosing 3004.90.9252 as the best match, and I'm not confident about it. I have seen it listed as "Other: Other," but I believe 3004.90.9244 is for cardiovascular drugs. In some earlier schedules, 3004.90.9235 was "Hypotensive agents" and I don't think that line is current, so I'm going with 3004.90.9244.

